  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...A few chances for rain through the weekend, but\nno hazardous weather expected between Wednesday and Monday at \nthis time.\n\nAn upper low over the Northeast US will linger through Friday\nbefore moving to the northeast over the weekend. There are\nchances of a few showers or perhaps a thunderstorm in spots each\nday as daytime heating provides some instability. Friday still\nlooks like it could be the drier day.\n\nA broad upper-level trough will begin to form over the Ohio \nValley over the weekend. The trough may close off into a low,\nwith the trough axis likely remaining to the west into at least\nMonday. Cloud cover & precipitation chances will begin to \nincrease, particularly between Saturday evening and Sunday as \nthe low tracks offshore and towards the northeast. Severe \nprobabilities look low at this time, with a pretty weak wind \nfield aloft.\n\nTemperatures throughout the remainder of the week will be near\nto slightly below normal.",
